      "description": "<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/carol_mullen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Challenges and Breakthoughs of Female Department Chairs Across Disciplines in Higher Education</a> by Caren Mullen</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/debebe\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Transformational Learning in Women's Leadership Development Training</a> by Gelaye Debebe</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/derry_l_stufft\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Educational Leadership: Where are the Women?</a> by Derry Stufft</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/dr_glena_bower\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Effective Mentoring Relationship with Women in Sport: Results of a Meta-Ethnography</a> by Glenna Bower</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/dr_henry_dr_glenn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Balck Women Employed in the Ivory Tower: Connecting for Success</a> by Wilma Henry &amp; Nicole Glenn</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/dr_kuon_dr_weimar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wake Up Sleeping Beauty: Strong Heroines for Today's World</a> by Tricia Kuon &amp; Holly Weimar</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/dr_marilyn_byrd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Theorizing African American Women's Leadership Experiences: Socio-Cultural Theoretical Alternatives</a> by Marilyn Byrd</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/dr_slate_brown_tejeda-delgado\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Female High School Principals: Leadership Practices and Individual Traits</a> by Tony Horst Giese, John Slate, Michelle Stallone Brown, &amp; Carmen Tejeda-Delgado</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/lepkowski\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gender and the Career Aspirations, Professional Assets, and Personal Variables of Higher Education Administration</a> by Christine Lepkowski</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/lucy_bailey_final_file_10_11_2010\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"So Pleasant to be a School Maam\": The Civil War as an Educational Force for Women</a> by Lucy Bailey</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/no_10_vol_dr_valer_rosser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Principal Gender as Related to Campus Size, Level, and Academic Rating</a> by Valerie Roser, Michelle Brown, &amp; Cheryl Kelsey</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://issuu.com/advancingwomeninleadershipjournal/docs/robles-.pina\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gender Differences in Placement, Support, and Participation in Early School Programs for Urban Hispanic Students in Advanced Placement Courses</a> by Raul Hinojosa, Rebecca Robles-Pina, &amp; Stacey Edmonson</p>"
